  ("Why does my furnace stop working when it's really cold outside?", "A furnace that quits in deep cold usually has a frosted or snow-blocked vent pipe, a frozen condensate line, or a weak part that finally failed under a long run time. Clearing snow from the PVC pipes on the side of the house is safe to try yourself. Anything beyond that calls for a TSSA-certified technician."),
